# RETURN finishes; the game asks its questions -- the attributes,
# the sex, the name, the name again, the whole character, and a
# save offer -- and one final any-key begins the story. She is
# Voxam, Level 0 Female Peasant.
>
yes
female
Voxam
yes
yes
no
>

# Grubbo-by-the-Sea. The billboard advertises the Fields of
# Frotzen; the spenseweed heals; the driftwood is a "genu-ine
# shillelagh". The sailor's painting shows the galleon to come.
nw
read billboard
examine weeds
get weed
se
e
e
examine water
get driftwood
examine painting


# Into the pub: the rusty lantern by the stairs, the thrown dagger
# in the kitchen wall, the great onion by the cellar door.
w
s
get rusty lantern
open door
w
w
get dagger
wield dagger
w
examine onion
open cellar door
turn on lantern

# The Wine Cellar, seed 999's first random map. Charted so far:
#
#   Wine Cellar --sw-> Throne Room --w-> Reeking Room --w-> Musty Corridor
#        (up: locked)      (nest)             \--nw-> Bottom of Stack
#
# The crinkly scroll (always Refreshment) lies at the stairway
# bottom; its word on this seed is Squirp, and saying it
# refreshes the lantern and dagger. The rat-ant attacks at once
# and falls to the fifth dagger blow.
d
get scroll
read scroll
squirp
attack rat-ant
attack rat-ant
attack rat-ant
attack rat-ant
attack rat-ant

# Rest to full endurance before the crab: one point per waited
# turn.
wait
wait
wait
wait
wait
wait
wait

# The Throne Room. The discipline crab falls to the eighth blow
# -- the tiny crown drops with a PLINK, and the kill makes Voxam
# a Level 1 Female Peasant (endurance cap now 20). The nest hides
# the doubloon.
sw
attack crab
attack crab
attack crab
attack crab
attack crab
attack crab
attack crab
attack crab
get crown
search nest
get doubloon

# West to the Reeking Room, where this seed's wand-family item is
# a staff.
w
get staff


# The Musty Corridor's sickly gray moss IS the moss of Mareilon:
# the squeeze answers only "soft and pliant", but the itchy
# finger it leaves is the tell, and the +8 dexterity lands a few
# turns later with "a satisfying scratch" -- DX 18 becomes 26.
w
squeeze moss

# The Shadowy Stacks skeleton throttles whoever reaches for its
# amulet; one kick crumbles it. The full seed-999 cellar:
#
#   Wine Cellar --sw-> Throne --w-> Reeking --w-> Musty --nw-> Shadowy Stacks
#      (up: locked)                    |               |
#                                     nw------Bottom of Stack---n
#                                                  u -> Top of Stack
nw
take amulet
kick skeleton
take amulet
wear amulet

# Up the crates for the wine bottle (the climb wants Dex 15; the
# moss has us at 26), then back to the stairway.
se
n
u
get wine bottle
d
se
e
ne

# The door overhead locked itself, as promised. The wine bottle
# is a lens: through it the amulet reads "Watkin" -- seed 999's
# word -- and the weakened door breaks.
u
read amulet through bottle
watkin
break cellar door
u
turn off lantern

# "Been after this thing for years." The bottle buys the giant
# onion -- Act 1's milestone, and the key to everything east.
give bottle to cook


# Act 1 rests here, giant onion secured; the road east through
# Accardi and beyond is the next expedition. A clean quit keeps
# the replay silent.
quit
yes
